{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1526023-why-vampires-in-requiem-respect-the-masquerade-tradition","id":1526023,"title":"Why Vampires in Requiem respect the Masquerade Tradition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-27T17:30:56-08:00","id":1526023,"title":"Why Vampires in Requiem respect the Masquerade Tradition","content":"I understand the force behind the creation of Masquerade Tradition in VtM and all backstory with Inquisition, Anarch War and everthing else, but in Requiem the Traditions dont have a strong history behind, how make the Traditions more weight in the Requiem scenario?<br /> I think the Masquerade tradition may be someting in relation of hide to Hunters and Strix or something else.<br /> i dont no how make the Traditions in Requiem more important to scenario <br /> any thoughs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T18:11:19-08:00","id":1526026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1526023-why-vampires-in-requiem-respect-the-masquerade-tradition#post1526023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the force behind the creation of Masquerade Tradition in VtM and all backstory with Inquisition, Anarch War and everthing else, but in Requiem the Traditions dont have a strong history behind, how make the Traditions more weight in the Requiem scenario?<br /> I think the Masquerade tradition may be someting in relation of hide to Hunters and Strix or something else.<br /> i dont no how make the Traditions in Requiem more important to scenario<br /> any thoughs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Traditions in Requiem are not formal laws established in ther middle ages like in Masquerade. They are the spoken and written expression of patterns within the Beast and Blood. Older than the current covenants, middle ages, the roman empire and its Camarilla. It's instinct explained in a way the human side of the dead can claim as theirs, but of origins lost in time, imprinted on kindred nature and old as the Requiem itself.<br /> <br /> (At least that's how i remember it back in 1e, if things changed sometime between late 1e and 2e, i have no idea and anyone is free to correct me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T19:27:07-08:00","id":1526029,"title":"","content":"You respect the Masquerade because when you don't humans, who out number vampires thousands to one will kill you. And because your elders will kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T00:51:29-08:00","id":1526042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1526023-why-vampires-in-requiem-respect-the-masquerade-tradition?p=1526029#post1526029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You respect the Masquerade because when you don't humans, who out number vampires thousands to one will kill you. And because your elders will kill you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes i know but is lacking of lore in Traditions in Requiem in Masquerade we have strong motivation and history of inquisition behind <br /> <br /> In Requiem the explanation &quot;because humans and Elder will kill you&quot; is t\u00f4 simple and lame <br /> How create a little backstory to give more valor and weight to Traditions in Requiem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T02:24:04-08:00","id":1526045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1526023-why-vampires-in-requiem-respect-the-masquerade-tradition?p=1526042#post1526042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes i know but is lacking of lore in Traditions in Requiem in Masquerade we have strong motivation and history of inquisition behind<br /> <br /> In Requiem the explanation &quot;because humans and Elder will kill you&quot; is t\u00f4 simple and lame<br /> How create a little backstory to give more valor and weight to Traditions in Requiem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same way how you give weight to feeding scenes, Clan Banes, Touchstones, etc; make it personal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You were old and on death's door, so you accepted a new life. A half-life, but it's life right? Can you tell the same to your spouse and children? For the next few years, maybe. For the next decade?<br /> <br /> You accepted the Curse because you were a loner and an outcast, never fitting in with the 'normies'. Except that one friend you had. Can you tell them what you've become? Will they understand?<br /> <br /> You saw nothing, and nothing happened to you. It was just a drug addict with large teeth, you swear. Sunlight is painful to look at, but it's just photosensitivity you swear. It'll get okay, so don't make a fuss. Please.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now for the ST, the trick is tying all that to the game's main story, which I admit will be the hard part. But hey, so is the decades-old lore in WoD, so why the hell not here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T04:24:45-08:00","id":1526051,"title":"","content":"The traditions are basically just part of being a vampire.<br /> <br /> The Traditions as a tripartite code comes from the Camarilla of classical Rome... Though the first and second have been altered at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T11:58:57-08:00","id":1526073,"title":"","content":"I like to think that the beast has some part to play by eliminating threats to its security but mechanically I haven\u2019t integrated it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T21:07:29-08:00","id":1526152,"title":"","content":"As a bit of history: The Three Traditions <i>kind of </i>come from the Camarilla, but the Third Tradition is the only one modern Kindred share with the Romans. The Masquerade was something the Julii and the Propinqui used (presumably under a different name), but it was more an informal taboo than a law. I <i>believe </i>it's stated somewhere that the First and Second Traditions come from the Lancea et Sanctum (the Second is very much in keeping with their religion), replacing the ones the Julii used. But the idea of a Masquerade, in that it's about concealing that you, personally, are a vampire (it's not about whether vampires are real), is a concept as old as crime.<br /> <br /> Remember too that the Masquerade isn't just a law: it's built into the Kindred state of being as the Lost Visage (this is talked about in 1e, not as much in 2e). All three Traditions have a mechanical element: you lose a Humanity dot for the Embrace, you can conceal your nature more easily, and you suffer all kinds of downsides for diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-30-2023, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T11:02:48-08:00","id":1526239,"title":"","content":"In the first edition vampires in the reqiuem were hardwired from the moment of the embrace to keep themselves hidden from humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T03:11:53-08:00","id":1526271,"title":"","content":"Because for vampires the world is a<i> &quot;dark forest.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Without the masquerade they would make noise that would attract other predators (Vampires, Werewolf, Mages, Spirits, True Fae, Comic Horros etc...) or make the humans become the predator and demostrate why they are the apex species on planet earth. Even in VTM before the masquerade was internatinally enforced by the camarilla, vampires hid their true nature from humans: It was the secrecy of blood.<br /> <br /> Vampires self police themselves into compliance with the masquerade because without it chances are they suffer final death sooner than later. Also most of them like human society to some extend or are able to see their perks because they used to be human. The masquerade benefits everyone thus is normal it becomes a tradition across all vampires in the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Recommended video:</b><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xAUJYP8tnRE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xAUJYP8tnRE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xAUJYP8tnRE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xAUJYP8tnRE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T01:07:51-08:00","id":1526346,"title":"","content":"Aside from the obvious OOC answer of it being a major part of VTM and carrying over into VTR, the Tradition of the Masquerade just makes sense for Kindred. Whether it be out of pure self-interest, an inclination supernaturally hardwired into them from the moment of Embrace, or a relic of the old Roman Camarilla laws that survived into modern times, the Masquerade is common sense and it's served vampires quite well for millennia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T04:42:56-08:00","id":1526351,"title":"","content":"You need the Masquerade in order to have a world where vampires exist but humans don\u2019t know about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T08:20:24-08:00","id":1526360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1526023-why-vampires-in-requiem-respect-the-masquerade-tradition?p=1526351#post1526351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need the Masquerade in order to have a world where vampires exist but humans don\u2019t know about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed completely.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade just makes sense both from an OOC perspective (you need a world where vampires exist but humans are largely unaware about them) and in-universe perspective (humans being unaware vampires exist makes it easier for vampires to prey on them)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T11:16:19-08:00","id":1526366,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of the 1st Blade film where Frost was complaining to the leaders of Vampire society about the need to hide from humanity and seeing the elders just look at him at such ghastly horror as they knew that a war with humanity would be the end of them and how Deacon Frost couldn't grasp such a simple idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T19:18:32-08:00","id":1526388,"title":"","content":"Most vampire games I've played in, the players didn't seem to know what the masquerade was as they could constantly break it; they'd feed in the open, kill dozens of police-officers and there were never any consequences to their actions. A storyteller shouldn't always have consequences for every breech; they're a ST, not the moral, ethics-police. They should make a roll. <br /> <br /> The Traditions need to be enforced by other vampires to be effect; sure, mortals can be deadly, but, they can't hunt vampire like another one of their kind. And I'm in agreement; the Elders will kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T11:58:37-08:00","id":1526460,"title":"","content":"A shame that the ST didn't crack down and have real consquences for such actions. Precinct 13 had a section on that killing cops has serious blowback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T22:13:36-08:00","id":1526582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1526023-why-vampires-in-requiem-respect-the-masquerade-tradition?p=1526360#post1526360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed completely.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade just makes sense both from an OOC perspective (you need a world where vampires exist but humans are largely unaware about them) and in-universe perspective (humans being unaware vampires exist makes it easier for vampires to prey on them)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly yeah, I don't see how it can even be a question in dark ages maybe powerful vampires could rule a village maybe even a county or duchy, but if humanity as a whole knew that vampires existed in the modern day the consequences would be horrific for kindred. Even the most durable kindred would be at risk with some modern weaponry, like say dragonsbreath rounds for example, or 20 mm cannons. <br /> <br /> I could see temperature scans like what we had in covid becoming common at say government buildings, thermal cameras, etc... Even though a vampire can get around that with blush of life it still would cost considerable blood to keep it up all night unless you took that ordo dracul coil anyway. <br /> <br /> <br /> Not to mention single captured kindred could be researched, and potentially made to demonstrate their abilities which could have leading scientists and others looking into ways to circumvent them. <br /> <br /> Scholarly journals, news sources, warnings it would be a very bad thing for kindred society even if they could avoid suspicions since many would be looking for things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T22:23:15-08:00","id":1526583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1526023-why-vampires-in-requiem-respect-the-masquerade-tradition?p=1526460#post1526460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A shame that the ST didn't crack down and have real consquences for such actions. Precinct 13 had a section on that killing cops has serious blowback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard agree here, I don't mind not giving internal consequences if you are a psychopath but external consequences are a must. If you kill cops you probably will be found especially if you kill dozens of them. The police tend to pursue cop killers rabidly and with many officers wearing body cams even with say the lost visage with that many angles they would be able to at least determine skin color, height, weight, and possibly hair color. If you left ammunition around they would also check for fingerprints, if there was snow mud or you stepped in blood they would get your shoe size as well. At the very least they would put up offers for information perhaps with a reward which may have other vampires try to turn you in since you are a masquerade risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T11:00:03-08:00","id":1526613,"title":"","content":"Makes me wonder Iguazu if the crew even bothered to read even the cliff notes version of the setting and being discrete is a good survival tool when you are outnumber greatly by the living no matter how strong your blood potency is and using the more potent levels of the Disciplines expend more energy and leave you helpless to defend yourself later from a smart adversary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T08:51:35-08:00","id":1529908,"title":"","content":"The Masquerade in Requiem is primarily about protecting the identities of individual vampires, rather than the existence of vampires in the abstract. Everyone following this rule allows vampire to feed and pursue their goals with minimal mortal interference, which is overall better for business, as it were.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s basically the concept of <i>omert\u00e0 </i>in organized crime: you don\u2019t have to like each other, but everybody in the life agrees to not talk to civilians, and especially not cops, about your or anyone else\u2019s business within that realm, because doing so just makes it harder for everyone to do that business. <br /> <br /> The Invictus are the self-appointed enforcers of this rule, but all the covenants can appreciate the usefulness of being able to move through the mortal world undetected, and keeping the hunter threat mostly small and disorganized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T11:40:07-08:00","id":1529925,"title":"","content":"It's mutual self interest and safety for the Kindred of VTR to stay hidden from the humans and that supersedes personal feelings towards each other or how the Convenats regard each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}